          "distinct": true,
          "id": "fda4a1a2d7b154661f2ce0ef0abfb47fcb92b94d",
          "message": "Rewrite aligned_alloc\n\nIt appears more common for implementations to request a chunk large\nenough to ensure a suitably-aligned sub-region and then to free the\nunused portion. This is less likely to succeed, since it requires a\nlarger free space than strictly necessary, but it's simpler, and it\nkeeps malloc fast and small even if an aligned allocation is used, which\nis more important. It will also be considerably faster if we get\nconstant time free list traversal.",
          "timestamp": "2024-01-27T14:15:18-08:00",
          "tree_id": "2f0735392f677c7c1b134ced427ba6fd813e78c3",
          "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos-sdk/commit/fda4a1a2d7b154661f2ce0ef0abfb47fcb92b94d"
